<Base title="For healthcare professionals" description="Information about the non-medical I Will Bloom journal for healthcare teams, charities and support organisations."><article class="prose"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / A thoughtful addition to everyday support.</nav><p class="eyebrow">For professionals & organisations</p><h1>A thoughtful addition to everyday support.</h1><p>I Will Bloom is a non-medical guided journal for people navigating cancer treatment and recovery. It offers reflective prompts, quiet activities and practical space for everyday life.</p><h2>What it offers</h2><p>The journal creates an optional place for personal reflection. Readers choose what they write, how often they use it and whether they share anything with others.</p><h2>Its boundaries</h2><p>The journal is not a clinical assessment, treatment, symptom-monitoring service or crisis resource. It does not provide individual health guidance, and no clinical outcome is promised.</p><h2>Enquiries from your organisation</h2><p>Rachel welcomes enquiries from hospitals, clinics, charities, support groups and other organisations interested in the journal or bulk purchases.</p><p><a class="btn" href="mailto:connect@iwillbloom.com?subject=Professional%20journal%20enquiry">Contact Rachel →</a></p><h2>Professional perspectives</h2><p>Approved professional feedback will be added here after the exact wording, attribution and permission have been checked.</p></article></Base>